@.str.19 = private unnamed_addr constant [1468 x i8] c"\0AComputes the first intersection of the rays with the scene.\0A\0AArgs:\0A    rays (open3d.core.Tensor): A tensor with >=2 dims, shape {.., 6}, and Dtype\0A        Float32 describing the rays.\0A        {..} can be any number of dimensions, e.g., to organize rays for\0A        creating an image the shape can be {height, width, 6}. The last\0A        dimension must be 6 and has the format [ox, oy, oz, dx, dy, dz]\0A        with [ox,oy,oz] as the origin and [dx,dy,dz] as the direction. It is\0A        not necessary to normalize the direction but the returned hit distance\0A        uses the length of the direction vector as unit.\0A\0A    nthreads (int): The number of threads to use. Set to 0 for automatic.\0A\0AReturns:\0A    A dictionary which contains the following keys\0A\0A    t_hit\0A        A tensor with the distance to the first hit. The shape is {..}. If there\0A        is no intersection the hit distance is *inf*.\0A\0A    geometry_ids\0A        A tensor with the geometry IDs. The shape is {..}. If there\0A        is no intersection the ID is *INVALID_ID*.\0A\0A    primitive_ids\0A        A tensor with the primitive IDs, which corresponds to the triangle\0A        index. The shape is {..}.  If there is no intersection the ID is\0A        *INVALID_ID*.\0A\0A    primitive_uvs\0A        A tensor with the barycentric coordinates of the hit points within the\0A        hit triangles. The shape is {.., 2}.\0A\0A    primitive_normals\0A        A tensor with the normals of the hit triangles. The shape is {.., 3}.\0A\00", align 1
