@.str.35 = private unnamed_addr constant [1254 x i8] c"\0AComputes the signed distance to the surface of the scene.\0A\0AThis function computes the signed distance to the meshes in the scene.\0AThe function assumes that all meshes are watertight and that there are\0Ano intersections between meshes, i.e., inside and outside must be well\0Adefined. The function determines the sign of the distance by counting\0Athe intersections of a rays starting at the query points.\0A\0AArgs:\0A    query_points (open3d.core.Tensor): A tensor with >=2 dims, shape {.., 3},\0A        and Dtype Float32 describing the query_points.\0A        {..} can be any number of dimensions, e.g., to organize the\0A        query points to create a 3D grid the shape can be\0A        {depth, height, width, 3}.\0A        The last dimension must be 3 and has the format [x, y, z].\0A\0A    nthreads (int): The number of threads to use. Set to 0 for automatic.\0A\0A    nsamples (int): The number of rays used for determining the inside.\0A        This must be an odd number. The default is 1. Use a higher value if you\0A        notice sign flipping, which can occur when rays hit exactly an edge or\0A        vertex in the scene.\0A\0AReturns:\0A    A tensor with the signed distances to the surface. The shape is {..}.\0A    Negative distances mean a point is inside a closed surface.\0A\00", align 1
