@.str.37 = private unnamed_addr constant [1263 x i8] c"\0AComputes the occupancy at the query point positions.\0A\0AThis function computes whether the query points are inside or outside.\0AThe function assumes that all meshes are watertight and that there are\0Ano intersections between meshes, i.e., inside and outside must be well\0Adefined. The function determines if a point is inside by counting the\0Aintersections of a rays starting at the query points.\0A\0AArgs:\0A    query_points (open3d.core.Tensor): A tensor with >=2 dims, shape {.., 3},\0A        and Dtype Float32 describing the query points.\0A        {..} can be any number of dimensions, e.g., to organize the\0A        query points to create a 3D grid the shape can be\0A        {depth, height, width, 3}.\0A        The last dimension must be 3 and has the format [x, y, z].\0A\0A    nthreads (int): The number of threads to use. Set to 0 for automatic.\0A\0A    nsamples (int): The number of rays used for determining the inside.\0A        This must be an odd number. The default is 1. Use a higher value if you\0A        notice errors in the occupancy values. Errors can occur when rays hit\0A        exactly an edge or vertex in the scene.\0A\0AReturns:\0A    A tensor with the occupancy values. The shape is {..}. Values are either 0\0A    or 1. A point is occupied or inside if the value is 1.\0A\00", align 1
